summary:
  The way back from a calibration sets every speaker's level again,
  whether this run had parked it or not.

history:
  That was right for as long as every run parked every speaker. A run
  that is called off while it is still asking for levels parks some of
  them or none, and the level it puts back is "what I read, or the park
  if I read nothing". For a speaker it never got to, that is 55 %: a
  cancel pressed in the first second would leave the speakers it had not
  reached at the measuring level, with no run left to undo it. Each
  speaker is put back under the flag its own park set.

target:
  package/contents/ui/CalibLogic.js

find:
          restore += " [ -n \"$k" + si + "\" ] && pactl set-sink-volume \"$s" + si + "\" ${v" + si + ":-" + park + "%};";

replace:
          restore += " pactl set-sink-volume \"$s" + si + "\" ${v" + si + ":-" + park + "%};";

expect:
  Killed by tests/test_calibrate_cancel.py::test_cancel_during_the_first_query_parks_nothing_and_starts_nothing.
  Line-neutral.
